# Agent tooling — never published, never reviewed here. The one exception is the
# project's own review skill: the CI checks it out and invokes it as /mormot-review,
# so it has to be tracked. Every other path under .claude/ stays out, including the
# synced personal skills.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/mormot-review/
.codex/
.agents/
.bmad-loop/
.tokensave/
_bmad/
_bmad-output/

# Generated audio editions. Tens of megabytes each and rewritten daily, so a
# tracked copy would add a new blob to history every morning — about 25 GB a
# year. They are served from site/medias/ locally and belong on object storage
# in production; build_site.py simply offers whatever is present.
site/medias/
.review-tmp/
parts/
